Today is Wednesday.
I come back from the office in the evening.
I go into the building's lobby.
My neighbour Asha is standing there.
She sees me and smiles.
"Hello Maya, how are you?" she asks.
"I am well, Asha."
"And you?" I ask.
"I am fine too," she says.
"What are you doing this Saturday?" Asha asks.
"I am always at home on Saturday mornings," I answer.
"Shall we go out for coffee on Saturday?" she asks.
"This is a very good idea," I say.
I work in the office every day.
Therefore, I sometimes like to go out.
"At what time shall we meet?" I ask her.
"Shall we meet at eleven o'clock?" Asha asks.
"At eleven o'clock in the morning?" I ask.
"Yes, on Saturday morning at eleven o'clock," she says.
"Okay, we will meet on Saturday," I say happily.
I say 'yes' to her, but I do not look at my calendar.
